UID:35cf2eb2bc4aca23@role-civil-litigation-appellate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 11/12/2026: Urgent Notice: Outlook Outage Nov
 . 12\, 2026
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome
 \n→\nNews & Announcements\nUrgent Notice: Outlook Outage Nov. 12\, 2026\
 nDate:\n11/12/2026\nThe Judicial Branch experienced an email outage on Thu
 rsday\, November 12\, 2026 that began at approximately 1:00 p.m. and laste
 d through Friday\, November 13\, 2026 at approximately 7:00 a.m. The Judic
 ial Branch's email outage was part of the larger Microsoft Outlook outage 
 that spread throughout North America.\nFor anyone who filed a request for 
 a protection order by email after 12:30 p.m. on Thursday\, November 12\, 2
 026\, your request may not have been received by the courts. Please consid
 er resubmitting your filing by email or file a paper copy with the court.\
 nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13367403
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13367403
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:19fc7a0ef07febdd@role-civil-litigation-appellate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 11/2/2026: Judicial Branch Issues Amendment t
 o Administrative Order on the Maine Rules of Electronic Court Systems (MRE
 CS)\, Effective November 2\, 2026
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome
 \n→\nNews & Announcements\nJudicial Branch Issues Amendment to Administr
 ative Order on the Maine Rules of Electronic Court Systems (MRECS)\, Effec
 tive November 2\, 2026\nDate:\n11/2/2026\nThe Maine Judicial Branch announ
 ced today that an Administrative Order on rules and procedures applicable 
 to Maine eCourts and eFiling has been amended regarding the use of non-Jud
 icial Branch court forms when one has been provided by the court.\nAO JB 2
 0-03 (A. 11-26)\nwas adopted in 2020 to provide guidance on the applicabil
 ity of the Maine Rules of Electronic Court Systems (MRECS) during the tran
 sitional period during the implementation of Maine eCourts and electronic 
 filing when there are conflicts between MRECS and other Judicial Branch ru
 les and administrative orders.\nNew Section I.C. of JB 20-20 provides that
  "[i]f an applicable court-approved form exists and is available to the pu
 blic\, the parties must use it" and further adds the following requirement
 :\n"If a filer does not use a form\, the filer must include a brief explan
 ation in a cover letter accompanying the submission that indicates the exi
 sting form is not suitable."\nBarbara Cardone\, Director of Legal Affairs 
 and Public Relations explained the reason for the amendment. "The reason f
 or the amendment is to increase the efficiency of reviewing eFiling submis
 sions. eFilers who submit non-Judicial Branch-approved court forms can avo
 id having their submission rejected by including an explanatory cover lett
 er with the eFiling. We hope this clarification helps the eFiling and lega
 l community's smooth transition to eFiling and Maine eCourts."\nAO JB 20-0
 3 (A. 11-26) has been posted on the Administrative Orders page of the Judi
 cial Branch website at\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/adminorders/index.htm
 l\nSupporting documents\nPress Release (PDF)\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov
 /news/article.html?id=13365673
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13365673
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a37316cc847d4dc6@role-civil-litigation-appellate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261029
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 10/29/2026: Judicial Branch Announces Procedu
 re for Emergency Case Filings Regarding Elections
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome
 \n→\nNews & Announcements\nJudicial Branch Announces Procedure for Emerg
 ency Case Filings Regarding Elections\nDate:\n10/29/2026\nAUGUSTA\, Maine.
  The Maine Judicial Branch announced the procedure for emergency case fili
 ngs regarding elections to be held on November 3\, 2026.\nProcedure for El
 ection Filings\nIn order to expedite the review of filings\, Superior Cour
 t Chief Justice Robert Mullen and District Court Chief Judge Brent Davis i
 ssued a\nstanding order on October 28th\nrequiring\nall filings pertaining
  to the November 3 election and filed between Friday\, October 30\, 2026\,
  at 4:00 pm and Tuesday\, November 3\, 2026\, at 9:00 pm to be filed on pa
 per at the clerk's office.  Filers should NOT use the eFile Maine system\n
 for these emergency filings.\nFilings submitted on paper will be reviewed 
 immediately by a clerk and can be directed to the appropriate justice for 
 timely review.  Filers are also encouraged to put their cell phone numbers
  or emergency telephone numbers (where they can be reached after hours) on
  their filings.\nState Courts Open Late on November 3\nThe state courthous
 es in Bangor\, Augusta and Portland will be open until 9:00 p.m. for the p
 urpose of accepting and acting on emergency paper filings regarding electi
 ons.  A judge\, a clerk and a marshal will be on duty at each courthouse.\
 nAvailability of Documents to the Media\nAll public documents related to e
 lection filings will be posted on the high-profile page of the Judicial Br
 anchs public website as soon as is practicable.\nSupporting documents\nPre
 ss Release (PDF)\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=133656
 33
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13365633
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
