       may bill only for the legal stage with the higher hourly cap—not t
 he combined hourly cap of the concurrent legal stages.) \n Summary Prelimi
 nary Hearing (10 hrs)  \n Jeopardy Hearing\n (20 hrs) \n Judic\nial Review
  / Permanency Planning \n      Hea\nring (15 hrs) \n Termi\nnation of Pare
 ntal Rights Hearing (20 hrs ) \n Cease Reunific\nation Hearing (15 hrs) \n
  Contested Permanency Guardianship Hearing  \n       (22 M.R.S. § 4038-C)
  (15 hrs)   \n Cont\nested Child Placement Hearing (22 M.R.S. \n§ 4005-H(
 2)) (15 hrs)\n Dismissal of Child Protection Action (15 hrs) \nDismissal i
 ncludes attendance at uncontested adoption \nhearing on (mm/dd/yyyy)    \n
 (Please see Administrative Order JB-05-05.)\n Release of a GAL from an Ord
 er of Appointment (15 hrs) \n Law Court Appeal \n This voucher includes up
  to 10 additional hours for a summary \npreliminary hearing because a prel
 iminary protection order was \ngranted subsequent to case initiation. (Ple
 ase see Administrative \nOrder JB-05-05.)\nDATE STAGE COMPLETED: (mm/dd/yy
 yy): \n Other Type of Case. Please check the applicable type of case (20 h
 rs\; you must attach a copy of your appointment order.)     \n Juvenile Ma
 tter \n Family Matter – Guardianship \n Family Matter – Adoption \n Fa
 mily Matter – Termination of Parental Rights\, Title 19-A \n Guardian fo
 r Minor or Incompetent Person\, M.R. Civ. P. 17(b) \nTOTAL HOURS: (In 0.1 
 increments. You must attach itemization of time.) \n hrs at $150/hour (aft
 er March 1\, 2023) = Total Hourly Fee $ \n VOUCHER EXCEEDS NUMBER OF ALLOW
 ABLE HOURS. The voucher exceeds the maximum hours allowed by JB-05-5. \n A
  motion to exceed the maximum allowed hours was filed on (mm/dd/yyyy):    
  . \nhttps://mjbportal.courts.maine.gov/CourtForms/FormsLists/DownloadForm
 ?strFormNumber=CV-FM-JV-PB-PC-024
