UID:94e9accbf66536e4@role-civil-litigation-appellate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172353Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Protection from Abuse/Harassment Filing Codes
  and Lead Documents
DESCRIPTION:MAINE JUDICIAL BRANCH \n \nRev. 10/26                         
              Page 1 of 2  \n \nPROTECTION FROM ABUSE AND PROTECTION FROM H
 ARASSMENT \nFILING CODES AND LEAD DOCUMENTS \n \neFileMaine is the platfor
 m attorneys and parties use to electronically file (eFile) documents and p
 erform other tasks \nonline in court cases where eFiling is available. eFi
 leMaine users must register for an account and provide an email \naddress 
 to be used for eService\, provide payment details or an exemption from pay
 ing filing fees (if applicable)\, and \nagree to terms of use. \n \nVisit 
 the eFileMaine webpage for information on account set up\, registration\, 
 user guides\, and ways to contact technical \nsupport.  \n \nThis form is 
 a brief overview of the filing codes and lead documents that must be selec
 ted to properly start or eFile into \na protection from abuse or protectio
 n from harassment case in eFileMaine.  \n \nPLEASE NOTE: Documents marked 
 below as “REQUIRED” must be submitted. Filings that do not include all
  requirements \nwill be rejected pursuant to M.R. Civ. P. 5(f) and M.R.E.C
 .S. 35(D).  \n \n1. PROTECTION FROM ABUSE – CASE INITIATION \na. Case In
 formation: \n  Case category – Family \n  Case type – Protection from 
 Abuse  \n \nb. Filings/Lead Documents: \ni. Complaint (PA-001) – REQUIRE
 D \n[Filing Document – Complaint – Filed]  \n \nPLEASE NOTE: The follo
 wing documents must be completed and uploaded as separate attachments to \
