DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Standing Order: Standing Order Requiring Pape
 r Filing for Election Day 2026 Emergency Matters
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE       SUPERIOR COURT \nDISTRICT COURT \n \n  \n
 STANDING ORDER REQUIRING \nPAPER FILING FOR ELECTION DAY \n2026 EMERGENCY 
 MATTERS \n \n \n The Maine Judicial Branch (MJB) is implementing the Maine
  eCourts \nsystem – including eFiling – statewide.1  EFileMaine is a p
 ractical and efficient \ndocument submission system already in use in many
  courts throughout the \nstate.  However\, because filings related to Elec
 tion Day may be uniquely time-\nsensitive\, to ensure timely processing\, 
 the MJB will require paper filing under \nthe limited circumstances descri
 bed below.   \n \n It is therefore ORDERED that any emergency Title 21-A f
 ilings related to \nElection Day 2026 filed between 4:00 p.m. on Friday\, 
 October 30\, 2026\, and \n9:00 p.m. on Tuesday\, November 3\, 2026\, must 
 be by paper\, unless otherwise \nordered.2 \n \nIt is further ORDERED that
  the Maine Rules of Electronic Court Systems \nare SUSPENDED to the extent
  necessary to give effect to this order.   \n \n \n \nDated: 10/28/2026   
 _____/s/______________________   \n       Chief Justice Robert E. Mullen \
 n \n \n \nDated: 10/28/2026   ___/s/_______________________   \n       Chi
 ef Judge Brent Davis \n \n1 Further information about the Maine eCourts sy
 stem is available at \nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/ecourts/index.html \n2
  Any Election Day 2026 filings filed by eFile during this period may not b
 e processed until the next business \nday after the election.\nhttps://www
 .courts.maine.gov/adminorders/so-election-day-procedure.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/adminorders/so-election-day-procedure.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:17826b6223eeac1c@role-civil-litigation-appellate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172323Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261119
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Seal Cove Auto Museum v. John J. Sanford et a
 l.
DESCRIPTION:MAINE SUPREME JUDICIAL COURT Reporter of Decisions \nDecision:
   2026 ME 110 \nDocket: BCD-25-555 \nArgued: October 8\, 2026 \nDecided:  
 November 19\, 2026 \n \nPanel:  STANFILL\, C.J.\, and MEAD\, CONNORS\, DOU
 GLAS\, and LIPEZ\, JJ.  \n \n \nSEAL COVE AUTO MUSEUM \n \nv. \n \nJOHN J.
  SANFORD et al. \n \n \nLIPEZ\, J. \n[¶1]  In 2020\, the parties to this 
 appeal\, Seal Cove Auto Museum \, the \nRichard C. Paine\, Jr.\, Automobil
 e Collection Charitable Trust  (the Trust or the \nCharitable Trust)\, and
  the Trust’s trustees\, John J. Sanford and John  Peabody \nMonks Higgin
 s (the Trustees) \, entered into a settlement agreement and an \namended r
 elationship agreement to resolve a legal dispute.  In 2022\, after the \nT
 rust announced a plan to donate $1\,000\,000 to the Owls Head Transportati
 on \nMuseum\, Seal Cove filed a motion to enforce\, arguing that the donat
 ion to Owls \nHead violated the Trust’s and the Trustees’ obligations 
 under the agreements.  \nAfter a bench trial\, t he Business and Consumer 
 Docket ( Duddy\, J.) denied the \nmotion\, and Seal Cove now appeals\, pri
 marily asserting  that the trial court \nmisinterpreted relevant provision
 s of the amended relationship agreement and \n \n \n2 \nerred in finding t
 hat the Trust had not breached that agreement.  Upon review \nof Seal Cove
 ’s arguments\, we conclude that they lack merit\, and we accordingly \na
 ffirm. \nI.  BACKGROUND \n [¶2]  This is not the first time that we have 
 addressed an appeal involving \nthese parties.  As we explained in Attorne
 y General v. Sanford: \nRichard Paine Jr. established Seal Cove in 1963 an
 d the \nRichard C. Paine\, Jr.\, Automobile Collection Charitable Trust (t
 he \nTrust) in 1986.  The Trust and Seal Cove were established to \nmainta
 in and display Paine ’s large collection of antique \nautomobiles.  Foll
 owing Paine's death in 2007\, the Trust acquired \nmost of Paine ’s auto
 mobiles and an endowment to support \nmaintenance and display of the autom
 obile collection.  Sanford and \nHiggins presently serve as trustees of th
 e Trust. \n \n. . . The Declara\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/l
 awcourt/2026/26me110.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/lawcourt/2026/26me110.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
